Fire Tornados.text:
{{Breadcrumb Auto|parent=Environmental Conditions|overview=Conditions}}
{{DisambigMsg|the fire-based environmental condition|the Exostorm effect|Exostorm#Class_2{{!}}Class 2 Exostorms}}
{{Quote|{{Environmental Conditions|{{PAGENAME}}}}|Galactic War Map}}

'''Fire Tornados''' are an environmental condition that create occasional storms of Fire Tornados on [[Scorched Moor]] planets. which move slowly and (semi)randomly throughout the play area. An active Fire Tornado storm will activate the [[Intense Heat]] environmental condition for its duration, after which the condition will deactivate.

== Overview ==
[[File:ThreeFireTornadoesOnExtract.png|thumb|alt=Three Fire Tornados on extraction.|Three Fire Tornadoes on extract.]]
When spawned, each Fire Tornado will move around the map similar to an enemy patrol, with slightly more randomization.  Wherever the Fire Tornado goes, it will leave an immolating (30-meters long, 10-meters wide) trail of flames with the immolation-lifetime of 30-seconds.  Contact with the Fire Tornado or it's flame trail will result in any living entity making contact to be lit on fire; structure-entities such as [[A/MLS-4X Rocket Sentry]] won't get immolated but will suffer and won't survive the base-fire-damage without health upgrade from [[Advanced Construction]]. Immolated [[Helldiver]]s can extinguish themselves by performing a dive.

While Fire Tornadoes are active on the map, the [[Intense Heat]] environmental condition will be active as well.

While most certainly very deadly and destructive to Helldivers and their stratagems, the Fire Tornado itself lacks demolition force, leaving structures in their pristine conditions (E.G. fences).

=== Dealing with Fire Tornadoes ===
* Fire Tornadoes can go anywhere an enemy NOT chasing after a [[Helldiver]] can walk. Climbing on a rocky cliff should keep a player safe from said tornadoes.
** This can best be seen within [[Cities]].  As patrols tend to stick to the roads, so will the Fire Tornadoes.  Helldivers will find themselves to be safe on the buildings.
* Should a Helldiver be unable to avoid the trail of flames, they should quickly dive to extinguish themselves.

== Trivia ==
* The name for the in-game effect uses ''Tornados'', the less common plural spelling of Tornado. This spelling originates from Spanish and has always been less popular than ''Tornadoes''.

== Change History ==
{{Change History Head}}
{{Change History Update|1.003.002|changes=
Undocumented fix
* Fixed the displacement issue of the Fire Tornados trails. The trails are now once more properly anchored to tornados itself rather than being invisible and immolating unsuspecting victims located other side of the map while the visually observed trails were only a visual nuisance.
}}
{{Change History Update|1.001.201|changes=
Changes
* Light intensity slightly reduced during the Fire Tornado weather effect.
}}
{{Change History Update|1.001.100|changes=
Changes
* Arid planets (similar to the Hellmire planet) will now only have the [[Intense Heat]] modifier active during fire tornado storms.
}}
{{Change History Update|1.000.400|changes=
Changes
* Fire tornados have had their behavior changed, they should no longer feel like they actively respond to player movement, and should move more randomly.
* While a fire tornado storm takes place, enemy vision is reduced. Player vision is unaffected.
}}
{{Change History Update|1.000.103|changes=
Changes
* Now spawns less frequently during missions.
}}

